    <script type="application/ld+json">
      {"@context":"http://schema.org","@graph":[{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Securities and Futures Commission (SFC)","url":"https://hk.linkedin.com/company/securities-and-futures-commission"},"datePublished":"2026-10-07T11:05:24.863Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":37},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_sfc-activity-7513555074501996544-cHYK","text":"𝗦𝗙𝗖 𝘁𝗼 𝗲𝗻𝗵𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲 𝗛𝗼𝗻𝗴 𝗞𝗼𝗻𝗴’𝘀 𝗿𝗲𝘁𝗮𝗶𝗹 𝗳𝘂𝗻𝗱 𝗿𝗲𝗴𝗶𝗺𝗲\n \nThe #SFC will introduce measures to strengthen the regulatory framework for SFC-authorised retail funds, as outlined in its consultation conclusions published today.\n \nThe enhancements to the Code on Unit Trusts and Mutual Funds (UT Code) will take effect in November 2026. They reflect the SFC’s commitment to investor protection and aligning Hong Kong’s regulatory framework with international standards.\n \nKey changes include introducing a Value-at-Risk (VaR) approach to manage retail funds’ derivative exposure, supporting a wider range of fund strategies and products.\n \nOther measures will streamline requirements for management company acceptability and feeder funds, giving fund managers greater operational flexibility. Enhanced safeguards for liquidity risk management and money market funds will also strengthen the resilience of Hong Kong’s retail fund market.\n \nA 12-month transition period will generally apply to existing SFC-authorised funds from the effective date of the revised UT Code. The SFC will publish supplementary guidance, FAQs and revised templates in the coming months to support the transition.\n \nRead the press release for details: https://lnkd.in/eW7yjhKH","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_sfc-activity-7513555074501996544-cHYK"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Securities and Futures Commission (SFC)","url":"https://hk.linkedin.com/company/securities-and-futures-commission"},"datePublished":"2026-10-06T12:26:16.742Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":8},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_project-ensemble-report-activity-7513213036896366592-c4Sk","text":"The #SFC welcomes the publication of the Project Ensemble Business Use Case Report by the HKMA. The report highlights valuable insights gained from industry experimentation under the Project Ensemble Sandbox and outlines the next steps towards commercialisation. \n\nAs a co-lead of the asset management tokenisation initiatives under Project Ensemble, the SFC has worked closely with participating financial institutions to explore innovative use cases and advance the practical application of tokenisation. \n\nThe SFC has also contributed to the development of the Project Ensemble Taxonomy. This shared taxonomy of digital finance terms is expected to establish a common understanding of key concepts, which will enable more effective cross-sector collaboration.\n\nThe SFC will continue to push forward initiatives that support the sustainable development of Hong Kong's digital finance ecosystem.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_project-ensemble-report-activity-7513213036896366592-c4Sk"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Securities and Futures Commission (SFC)","url":"https://hk.linkedin.com/company/securities-and-futures-commission"},"datePublished":"2026-10-06T12:18:53.839Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":12},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_sfc-activity-7513211179226320896-lrhq","text":"Hong Kong’s securities industry recorded total net profits of $51.7 billion in the first half of this year, up by a solid 21% over the prior six months, according to the #SFC’s financial review of the securities industry. \n\nThe strong earnings growth was supported by robust trading activity and growing client participation for securities brokers. Their total value of transactions jumped 24% half-on-half to a record $149 trillion for the first six months of 2026, while the number of active clients increased 10% to around 5.7 million as of June.\n\nRead the press release (https://lnkd.in/g-HtcCEv) and full report (https://lnkd.in/gJ5cvruK) for more details.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_sfc-activity-7513211179226320896-lrhq"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Securities and Futures Commission (SFC)","url":"https://hk.linkedin.com/company/securities-and-futures-commission"},"datePublished":"2026-09-30T12:44:44.540Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":20},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_sfc-activity-7511043356144287744-zgG8","text":"The #SFC and Securities Commission Malaysia today launched a single submission mechanism to facilitate simultaneous IPO listings in Hong Kong and Malaysia, a timely follow-up to the memorandum of understanding signed by the two regulators two months ago.\n\nUnder the simplified dual IPO listing framework, only a single listing application submission with a single listing document is required of an applicant seeking a primary listing on either the Main Board of the Stock Exchange of Hong Kong or the Main Market of Bursa Malaysia Securities Berhad, together with a simultaneous secondary listing on the other market. In addition, dedicated dual-listing review teams and coordinated regulatory review process will provide applicants and their advisers with direct points of contact, as well as align vetting timelines, minimise duplication, streamline queries and ensure seamless cross-agency handling throughout the listing process. \n\nBy reducing regulatory duplication and compliance costs, the new arrangement will promote simultaneous IPO listings in both markets and hence deepen market connectivity between Hong Kong and Malaysia.\n \n For more details, read the press release (https://lnkd.in/gyjKVvHq) and the circular on the single submission arrangement for dual listings (https://lnkd.in/gDUSnXD6)","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_sfc-activity-7511043356144287744-zgG8"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Securities and Futures Commission (SFC)","url":"https://hk.linkedin.com/company/securities-and-futures-commission"},"datePublished":"2026-09-29T11:16:06.348Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":9},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_sfc-activity-7510658662160424962-Jpno","text":"The #SFC’s Takeovers Bulletin (September 2026) explains that the SFC takes a pragmatic, fact-based approach to assessing whether government or state-owned entities are concert parties under the Takeovers Code and Share Buy-backs Code. Common state ownership alone is not decisive; governance, decision-making, voting patterns and relevant arrangements will be considered. \n\nHong Kong’s uncertificated securities market regime will launch on 16 November 2026. Offerors and advisers should factor it into transaction timetables and clearly explain acceptance and share-return procedures, including that untaken shares in a completed partial offer may be returned in uncertificated form.\n\nRead the issue for more details: https://lnkd.in/enUeqvHq","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_sfc-activity-7510658662160424962-Jpno"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Securities and Futures Commission (SFC)","url":"https://hk.linkedin.com/company/securities-and-futures-commission"},"datePublished":"2026-09-29T10:23:14.681Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":12},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_sfc-activity-7510645359224922113-5err","text":"The #SFC cautions the public against instant text messages and emails from scammers impersonating its senior executives.\n\nThe SFC stresses that these messages are fraudulent. The claims about the SFC or the Investor Compensation Company Limited making compensation for investment losses are entirely false.\n\nThe SFC reminds the public to stay vigilant against imposter scams, as fraudsters often use easily accessible photos as their profile pictures or claim to be SFC employees to gain the trust of victims and lure them into scams. The SFC reiterates that members of the public should never transfer funds or disclose personal information to anyone claiming to be an SFC employee via instant messaging apps or social media.\n\nRefer to the SFC's Alert List (https://lnkd.in/gUuDceAi) and Anti-Deception Coordination Centre’s webpage (https://lnkd.in/gb7khTrq) for latest alerts.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_sfc-activity-7510645359224922113-5err"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Securities and Futures Commission (SFC)","url":"https://hk.linkedin.com/company/securities-and-futures-commission"},"datePublished":"2026-09-28T11:53:55.855Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":82},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_%F0%9D%97%9C%F0%9D%97%BB%F0%9D%97%B1%F0%9D%98%82%F0%9D%98%80%F0%9D%98%81%F0%9D%97%BF%F0%9D%98%86-%F0%9D%98%80%F0%9D%97%B2%F0%9D%97%BA%F0%9D%97%B6%F0%9D%97%BB%F0%9D%97%AE%F0%9D%97%BF-%F0%9D%97%BC%F0%9D%97%BB-%F0%9D%98%80%F0%9D%97%B0-activity-7510305793297014785-0VfZ","text":"𝗜𝗻𝗱𝘂𝘀𝘁𝗿𝘆 𝘀𝗲𝗺𝗶𝗻𝗮𝗿 𝗼𝗻 𝘀𝗰𝗮𝗺 𝗽𝗿𝗲𝘃𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗰𝘆𝗯𝗲𝗿𝘀𝗲𝗰𝘂𝗿𝗶𝘁𝘆\n\nThe SFC today hosted a Brokers’ Forum, “Defend Your Business, Outsmart the Scammers”, bringing together over 600 industry participants to exchange insights on the latest supervisory observations and regulatory updates on cybersecurity and anti-scam measures.\n\nThe forum featured insights from the SFC, law enforcement and industry representatives on strengthening cyber resilience, taking joint action against financial scams in the brokerage sector, and briefing on the SFC’s anti-scam outreach initiatives.\n\nSee the press release for details: https://lnkd.in/gTkbR-tJ\n\nIn the photos:\n1. Executive Director of Intermediaries Dr Eric Yip delivering the welcome remarks\n2. Legislative Councillor for the Financial Services Functional Constituency Hon Robert Lee delivering the opening keynote address\n3. Hong Kong Police Force representative sharing insights on cyber resilience and scam prevention in the brokerage sector\n4. Panellists sharing their perspectives on collective action against financial scams during the panel discussion \n5. Briefing on the SFC’s anti-scam outreach initiatives \n6. Financial professionals attending the Brokers’ Forum","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_%F0%9D%97%9C%F0%9D%97%BB%F0%9D%97%B1%F0%9D%98%82%F0%9D%98%80%F0%9D%98%81%F0%9D%97%BF%F0%9D%98%86-%F0%9D%98%80%F0%9D%97%B2%F0%9D%97%BA%F0%9D%97%B6%F0%9D%97%BB%F0%9D%97%AE%F0%9D%97%BF-%F0%9D%97%BC%F0%9D%97%BB-%F0%9D%98%80%F0%9D%97%B0-activity-7510305793297014785-0VfZ"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Securities and Futures Commission (SFC)","url":"https://hk.linkedin.com/company/securities-and-futures-commission"},"datePublished":"2026-09-28T11:31:36.809Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":55},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_sfc-activity-7510300176931106816-qaDD","text":"𝗘𝗻𝗵𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲𝗱 𝗦𝗙𝗖-𝗔𝗙𝗥𝗖 𝗣𝗮𝗿𝘁𝗻𝗲𝗿𝘀𝗵𝗶𝗽: 𝗔 𝗟𝗶𝘃𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗙𝗿𝗮𝗺𝗲𝘄𝗼𝗿𝗸 𝘁𝗼 𝗕𝗼𝗹𝘀𝘁𝗲𝗿 𝗠𝗮𝗿𝗸𝗲𝘁 𝗖𝗼𝗻𝗳𝗶𝗱𝗲𝗻𝗰𝗲\n\nThe #SFC and the Accounting and Financial Reporting Council (AFRC) today entered into a new MoU to expand regulatory cooperation beyond the oversight of financial reporting and related audit work of listed entities. The new MoU covers the financial and compliance reporting by licensed corporations, SFC-licensed virtual asset service providers, SFC-authorised funds and registered open-ended fund companies, as well as the related audit and assurance work performed by their auditors.\n\nThe new MoU was signed today by the SFC’s CEO, Ms Julia Leung, and the AFRC’s CEO, Ms Janey Lai, in the presence of the SFC’s Chairman, Dr Kelvin Wong, and the AFRC’s Chairman, Dr David Sun, as well as other board members and senior executives of the SFC and the AFRC.\n\nSee the press release for details: https://lnkd.in/gxbycrCA","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_sfc-activity-7510300176931106816-qaDD"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Securities and Futures Commission (SFC)","url":"https://hk.linkedin.com/company/securities-and-futures-commission"},"datePublished":"2026-09-24T12:39:40.260Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":33},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_sfc-activity-7508867752703574016-atxu","text":"At today’s 10th Annual Institute on Corporate & Securities Law in Asia, Mr Michael Duignan, #SFC Executive Director of Enforcement, delivered a keynote address titled “A New Enforcement Philosophy: Less Trodden Pathways to Better Outcomes,” arguing that the SFC should pursue whichever lawful, workable solution delivers the fairest outcome fastest, rather than reaching for the same process out of habit. \n\nMr Duignan argued that enforcement works best when it fixes the structural drivers of misconduct before a case begins. He pointed to the SFC’s January circular to licensed corporations carrying out sponsor work, issued amid a more than 200% year-on-year rise in Hong Kong IPO proceeds. Firms were given clear deadlines to report principal-to-deal ratios and flag unqualified staff, well before problems could surface as enforcement cases.\n\nHe also discussed persistent intermediary misconduct at a brokerage, where cross-divisional action, licensing conditions, and the prospect of disciplinary proceedings led the firm to voluntarily surrender its licence and wind down, avoiding a drawn-out hearing process while protecting the market.\n\nTurning to minority shareholders, he highlighted the SFC’s settlements with PricewaterhouseCoopers Hong Kong ($1 billion) and Giordano International Limited (payments may be up to $1.5 billion). Both cases delivered redress to minority shareholders sooner than years of tribunal or court proceedings might have.\n\nMr Duignan also addressed the SFC’s power to direct trading suspensions for companies with unresolved concerns regarding their financial and operational status, describing it as a protection for the market as a whole. \nHe made it clear that the new enforcement philosophy is not against process, but against treating one particular process as the only legitimate route to a good outcome.\n\nRead the full speech here: https://lnkd.in/gvWuRfhq","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_sfc-activity-7508867752703574016-atxu"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Securities and Futures Commission (SFC)","url":"https://hk.linkedin.com/company/securities-and-futures-commission"},"datePublished":"2026-09-23T11:42:43.345Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":51},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_sfcs-strategic-action-plan-supports-hong-activity-7508491033261821952-guEu","text":"\u003CSFC’s Strategic Action Plan supports Hong Kong’s First Five-Year Plan and Policy Address in promoting capital market development\u003E \n\nThe SFC today unveiled a strategic action plan to support the implementation of Hong Kong’s First Five-Year Plan and the Policy Address through a series of short-, medium- and long-term measures to promote the high-quality development of Hong Kong’s capital markets. The purpose of the action plan is clear: to translate policy directions into market outcomes, and Hong Kong’s strengths into enduring market strength. \n\nThe action plan will focus on three priority areas: \n• strengthening Hong Kong’s renminbi and fixed income and currency market ecosystem; \n• broadening and deepening mutual market access; and \n• enhancing the efficiency, inclusiveness and quality of Hong Kong’s capital markets.\n\nThe SFC considers that Hong Kong’s First Five-year plan and the Policy Address provide a clear direction for the future development of Hong Kong’s financial markets. As a market regulator and a facilitator of market development, the SFC will actively support the HKSAR Government in promoting financial development and work with the industry to translate policy directions into market outcomes, thereby enhancing the depth, breadth and international competitiveness of Hong Kong’s financial markets.\n\nRead more:\n• Press release: https://lnkd.in/g3ApBCQM\n• The SFC’s Strategic Action Plan: https://lnkd.in/g56m4Fzg\n• Remarks by SFC’s Chairman Dr Kelvin Wong at news briefing: https://lnkd.in/gJH37ZfY\n• Remarks by SFC’s CEO Ms Julia Leung at news briefing: https://lnkd.in/gA4UPxVR","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/securities-and-futures-commission_sfcs-strategic-action-plan-supports-hong-activity-7508491033261821952-guEu"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"Organization","name":"Securities and Futures Commission (SFC)","url":"https://hk.linkedin.com/company/securities-and-futures-commission","address":{"type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"54/F, One Island East","addressLocality":"18 Westlands Road, Quarry Bay","addressCountry":"HK"},"description":"The Securities and Futures Commission (SFC) regulates the securities and futures markets in Hong Kong. Its responsibilities are to ensure that the markets operate fairly and efficiently, promote orderly development of the industry while protecting the interests of investors. \r\n\r\nThe SFC is a public body operating independent of the civil service. It is funded mainly by levies investors pay for securities and futures transactions and also by fees from licensees. Its core functions involve the licensing and supervision of intermediaries, ensuring compliance of laws specific to the industry, supervising the markets (including the infrastructure and trading activities), overseeing listing and takeovers matters and regulating investment products.","numberOfEmployees":{"value":724,"@type":"QuantitativeValue"},"logo":{"contentUrl":"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D560BAQHRla1d5CZrXg/company-logo_200_200/B56aDBjwDcHkAE-/0/1789953769944/securities_and_futures_commission_logo?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=Az5dGtzcgKFkwY1ptMkP90hJbPqUgshBlfl9jxiwHGw","description":"Securities and Futures Commission (SFC)","@type":"ImageObject"},"sameAs":"http://www.sfc.hk"}]}
    </script>
  
  
      
