  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="feed-reshare-content__commentary">Tokenisation offers a higher speed and a wider space. Commencing with experimentation on use cases, Project Ensemble introduces the industry to the concepts of the Super Innovator, the Super Connector and the Super Catalyst.

The HKMA is pleased to publish three key deliverables from Project Ensemble today: the 𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗷𝗲𝗰𝘁 𝗘𝗻𝘀𝗲𝗺𝗯𝗹𝗲 𝗕𝘂𝘀𝗶𝗻𝗲𝘀𝘀 𝗨𝘀𝗲 𝗖𝗮𝘀𝗲 𝗥𝗲𝗽𝗼𝗿𝘁, 𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗷𝗲𝗰𝘁 𝗘𝗻𝘀𝗲𝗺𝗯𝗹𝗲 𝗜𝗻𝘁𝗲𝗿𝗼𝗽𝗲𝗿𝗮𝗯𝗶𝗹𝗶𝘁𝘆 𝗦𝘁𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗿𝗱, and 𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗷𝗲𝗰𝘁 𝗘𝗻𝘀𝗲𝗺𝗯𝗹𝗲 𝗧𝗮𝘅𝗼𝗻𝗼𝗺𝘆. The reports establish a solid foundation for the HKMA and the industry to develop the infrastructure for Hong Kong, thereby unlocking benefits incrementally. Together, they reflect the collaborative efforts of the HKMA, the Project Ensemble Architecture Community and industry participants to advance tokenisation use cases, interoperability and shared terminology.

📄𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗷𝗲𝗰𝘁 𝗘𝗻𝘀𝗲𝗺𝗯𝗹𝗲 𝗕𝘂𝘀𝗶𝗻𝗲𝘀𝘀 𝗨𝘀𝗲 𝗖𝗮𝘀𝗲 𝗥𝗲𝗽𝗼𝗿𝘁
Summarising the business use cases experimented under Project Ensemble Sandbox since Q3 2024, the report captures key learnings and outlines the next steps towards commercialisation.

Report: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gusWHZbK?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gusWHZbK</a>

📄𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗷𝗲𝗰𝘁 𝗘𝗻𝘀𝗲𝗺𝗯𝗹𝗲 𝗧𝗮𝘅𝗼𝗻𝗼𝗺𝘆
The taxonomy that defines DLT-related terminologies and its interrelationships, supporting industry alignment and collaboration through a same language.

Report: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gHkiD2_K?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gHkiD2_K</a>

📄𝗣𝗿𝗼𝗷𝗲𝗰𝘁 𝗘𝗻𝘀𝗲𝗺𝗯𝗹𝗲 𝗜𝗻𝘁𝗲𝗿𝗼𝗽𝗲𝗿𝗮𝗯𝗶𝗹𝗶𝘁𝘆 𝗦𝘁𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗮𝗿𝗱
The standard provides a common technical foundation linking tokenised assets, tokenised money and central bank money to support interoperability and more efficient digital settlement.

Report: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gBSNRsKq?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card_reshare-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gBSNRsKq</a>

𝗪𝗵𝗮𝘁’𝘀 𝗡𝗲𝘅𝘁? 🔜
The HKMA remains committed to fostering a vibrant tokenisation ecosystem in Hong Kong. We invite banks, fintech pioneers, regulators and other stakeholders to collaborate in accelerating tokenisation initiatives from pilot to commercialisation.

Stay tuned for the next stage of Ensembleᵀᕽ!

