  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">Hong Kong’s securities industry recorded total net profits of $51.7 billion in the first half of this year, up by a solid 21% over the prior six months, according to the <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fsfc&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#SFC</a>’s financial review of the securities industry. 

The strong earnings growth was supported by robust trading activity and growing client participation for securities brokers. Their total value of transactions jumped 24% half-on-half to a record $149 trillion for the first six months of 2026, while the number of active clients increased 10% to around 5.7 million as of June.

Read the press release (<a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/g-HtcCEv?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/g-HtcCEv</a>) and full report (<a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gJ5cvruK?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gJ5cvruK</a>) for more details.</p>
