  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">The <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fsfc&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#SFC</a> cautions the public against instant text messages and emails from scammers impersonating its senior executives.

The SFC stresses that these messages are fraudulent. The claims about the SFC or the Investor Compensation Company Limited making compensation for investment losses are entirely false.

The SFC reminds the public to stay vigilant against imposter scams, as fraudsters often use easily accessible photos as their profile pictures or claim to be SFC employees to gain the trust of victims and lure them into scams. The SFC reiterates that members of the public should never transfer funds or disclose personal information to anyone claiming to be an SFC employee via instant messaging apps or social media.

Refer to the SFC's Alert List (<a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gUuDceAi?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gUuDceAi</a>) and Anti-Deception Coordination Centre’s webpage (<a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gb7khTrq?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gb7khTrq</a>) for latest alerts.</p>
