  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">𝗜𝗻𝗱𝘂𝘀𝘁𝗿𝘆 𝘀𝗲𝗺𝗶𝗻𝗮𝗿 𝗼𝗻 𝘀𝗰𝗮𝗺 𝗽𝗿𝗲𝘃𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗰𝘆𝗯𝗲𝗿𝘀𝗲𝗰𝘂𝗿𝗶𝘁𝘆

The SFC today hosted a Brokers’ Forum, “Defend Your Business, Outsmart the Scammers”, bringing together over 600 industry participants to exchange insights on the latest supervisory observations and regulatory updates on cybersecurity and anti-scam measures.

The forum featured insights from the SFC, law enforcement and industry representatives on strengthening cyber resilience, taking joint action against financial scams in the brokerage sector, and briefing on the SFC’s anti-scam outreach initiatives.

See the press release for details: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gTkbR-tJ?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gTkbR-tJ</a>

In the photos:
1. Executive Director of Intermediaries Dr Eric Yip delivering the welcome remarks
2. Legislative Councillor for the Financial Services Functional Constituency Hon Robert Lee delivering the opening keynote address
3. Hong Kong Police Force representative sharing insights on cyber resilience and scam prevention in the brokerage sector
4. Panellists sharing their perspectives on collective action against financial scams during the panel discussion 
5. Briefing on the SFC’s anti-scam outreach initiatives 
6. Financial professionals attending the Brokers’ Forum</p>
