  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">𝗘𝗻𝗵𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗲𝗱 𝗦𝗙𝗖-𝗔𝗙𝗥𝗖 𝗣𝗮𝗿𝘁𝗻𝗲𝗿𝘀𝗵𝗶𝗽: 𝗔 𝗟𝗶𝘃𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗙𝗿𝗮𝗺𝗲𝘄𝗼𝗿𝗸 𝘁𝗼 𝗕𝗼𝗹𝘀𝘁𝗲𝗿 𝗠𝗮𝗿𝗸𝗲𝘁 𝗖𝗼𝗻𝗳𝗶𝗱𝗲𝗻𝗰𝗲

The <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fsfc&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#SFC</a> and the Accounting and Financial Reporting Council (AFRC) today entered into a new MoU to expand regulatory cooperation beyond the oversight of financial reporting and related audit work of listed entities. The new MoU covers the financial and compliance reporting by licensed corporations, SFC-licensed virtual asset service providers, SFC-authorised funds and registered open-ended fund companies, as well as the related audit and assurance work performed by their auditors.

The new MoU was signed today by the SFC’s CEO, Ms Julia Leung, and the AFRC’s CEO, Ms Janey Lai, in the presence of the SFC’s Chairman, Dr Kelvin Wong, and the AFRC’s Chairman, Dr David Sun, as well as other board members and senior executives of the SFC and the AFRC.

See the press release for details: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gxbycrCA?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gxbycrCA</a></p>
