  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">&lt;SFC’s Strategic Action Plan supports Hong Kong’s First Five-Year Plan and Policy Address in promoting capital market development&gt; 

The SFC today unveiled a strategic action plan to support the implementation of Hong Kong’s First Five-Year Plan and the Policy Address through a series of short-, medium- and long-term measures to promote the high-quality development of Hong Kong’s capital markets. The purpose of the action plan is clear: to translate policy directions into market outcomes, and Hong Kong’s strengths into enduring market strength. 

The action plan will focus on three priority areas: 
• strengthening Hong Kong’s renminbi and fixed income and currency market ecosystem; 
• broadening and deepening mutual market access; and 
• enhancing the efficiency, inclusiveness and quality of Hong Kong’s capital markets.

The SFC considers that Hong Kong’s First Five-year plan and the Policy Address provide a clear direction for the future development of Hong Kong’s financial markets. As a market regulator and a facilitator of market development, the SFC will actively support the HKSAR Government in promoting financial development and work with the industry to translate policy directions into market outcomes, thereby enhancing the depth, breadth and international competitiveness of Hong Kong’s financial markets.

Read more:
• Press release: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/g3ApBCQM?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/g3ApBCQM</a>
• The SFC’s Strategic Action Plan: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/g56m4Fzg?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/g56m4Fzg</a>
• Remarks by SFC’s Chairman Dr Kelvin Wong at news briefing: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gJH37ZfY?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gJH37ZfY</a>
• Remarks by SFC’s CEO Ms Julia Leung at news briefing: <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/gA4UPxVR?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/gA4UPxVR</a></p>
